# TASK-AI-160 — root-cause fix for the network boundary (PR #508; branch feat/task-ai-160-agent-reach-v2)

History-scan blocker is solved by the squash (#508); remove the "retained commit b4631c7" limitation line in docs/product-spec/work-items/TASK-AI-160.md:146 and record `pnpm security:secrets` result instead.

1. WHERE: scripts/ai/research.mjs:851 runResearch (wrapper preflights the URL, then an external CLI re-fetches it).
   WRONG: target returns 200 to the preflight, then redirects to a private address during the CLI's own retrieval; the CLI follows it and private text comes back under the public URL.
   GOAL (R02, AC-AI-160-02/05): the boundary is enforced ON the retrieval itself. Do the retrieval in-process (defaultRetrieve): resolve DNS once, reject private/loopback/link-local/metadata IPs, connect to that pinned IP (custom `lookup`), `redirect: manual`, and re-validate every hop (max 5) before connecting. Use the CLI only to post-process text you already fetched, or drop it. A preflight-then-refetch design is not acceptable.
   VERIFY: test `redirect to private address during retrieval is refused` (local http server: 302 → 127.0.0.1) and `DNS rebinding between check and connect is refused`.
2. WHERE: scripts/ai/research.mjs:364 defaultRetrieve (`https.request` with default agent).
   WRONG: on Node 24 with NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 + HTTPS_PROXY set, the global agent sends traffic and operator proxy credentials through the proxy.
   GOAL (AC-AI-160-05): pass an explicit fresh `new https.Agent({ keepAlive:false })` / `http.Agent` for every request and never use globalAgent; spawned children get an env with HTTP(S)_PROXY, NO_PROXY, NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY and credentials removed.
   VERIFY: test `inherited proxy env is never used` (set env HTTPS_PROXY to a local listener, assert it receives zero connections).
Run: node --test scripts/ai/test/research.test.mjs, pnpm format:check, pnpm lint, pnpm run security:secrets.

## Required tools for this task (log each use in .oc/tools-used.txt, one line: tool + what for)
- ipaddr.js (installed) for private/loopback/link-local/metadata range checks — do not hand-write CIDR logic.
- node:http local test servers for redirect/rebinding tests (no network).
- Gitleaks via pnpm run security:secrets before commit.
- jcodemunch search for every call of defaultRetrieve/runResearch.

## Library to use (operator-approved 04/11; replaces hand-written code — pin an exact version, commit lockfile)
- request-filtering-agent (latest, by azu): `pnpm add -w request-filtering-agent`. Use `useAgent(url)` as the http(s) agent for EVERY hop of defaultRetrieve (it rejects private/loopback/link-local/metadata IPs at connect time, which also covers DNS rebinding). Follow redirects manually and pass a fresh agent per hop. This replaces the hand-written IP checks (ipaddr.js only if the library needs it).

- REUSE FIRST (operator 04/11): before writing any parser, sanitizer/redactor, URL/state sync, network guard, retry/queue, date/money/format helper or UI widget, search for a maintained library or an attached repo (manifest, context7.js, npm/GitHub) and USE it. Hand-write only if none fits, and say why in .oc/tools-used.txt ("no-lib: <reason>"). New dependencies are allowed when they are well-maintained (recent release, real user base, OSI licence), pinned to an exact version with the lockfile committed; never for auth/tenant/money logic without the Work Item naming it.

## root-cause (reference implementation, 04/11) — adapt, do not invent
Reference: github.com/jonathanong/ssrf-guard — validateUrl returns the resolved IPs so the socket is pinned to the validated IP (closes DNS-rebinding TOCTOU), redirects re-validated per hop. Use it directly if its Node requirement (>=24) matches our CI node; otherwise use request-filtering-agent and copy ssrf-guard's IP-pinning + per-hop redirect pattern.
Reference ALREADY CLONED read-only at C:/Users/gumac/AI/ref/ssrf-guard (do not clone), read the named parts, adapt to our files; respect licence and credit the source in a header comment; log reference + what was adapted in .oc/tools-used.txt.

## root-cause (USE THE PACKAGE, 04/11 12:00) — supersedes the reference sections above
`ssrf-guard@1.0.0` (MIT, by jonathanong, Node>=24 = our CI) is on npm. `pnpm add -w ssrf-guard@1.0.0`.
Replace defaultRetrieve's own DNS/IP/redirect/agent code in scripts/ai/research.mjs with ssrf-guard's safe fetch (it validates the URL, pins the socket to the validated IP, re-validates every redirect hop). Read its API in C:/Users/gumac/AI/ref/ssrf-guard/src/node/safe-fetch.mts and README.md. Keep request-filtering-agent only if ssrf-guard does not cover a case; otherwise remove it. Proxy env must still be stripped for children. Existing tests stay; add one test that a 302 to 127.0.0.1 is refused through ssrf-guard.
